(F,"fit of a dummy panel 27.35 x 12.8 x 0.8 in the pocket; coating colour and adhesion;","fit of a dummy panel 27.35 x 12.8 x 0.8 in the pocket; on the first body the slots, the motor window and the pocket depths with calipers and a depth gauge, read against the model (items 96 to 98); the bar certificate (item 99); the metal through each microphone pocket (item 77); coating colour, gloss and adhesion (item 105); five lap-shear strips of coated Ti-6Al-4V from the same coating batch, bonded and pulled, the break inside the adhesive (item 106);",LD+"'items 96, 97, 98', 'item 99', 'item 77', 'item 105', 'item 106'"),
(F,"2. Pocket clearance and depth for the screen panel (architecture 16.1 says 0.15 mm per side; the model uses 0.05): the design partner answers, then the maker confirms.","2. Pocket clearance and depth for the screen panel: decided, 0.05 mm per side as modelled (the 0.15 mm of architecture 16.1 is superseded; items 96 to 98); measured on the first body with a plug gauge.",LD+"'items 96, 97, 98'"),
(F,"7. Body variants for sizes other than US 9: the values per size are in the last section; the maker takes them from the STEP file per size once the parts helper exports it. The sealant of the floor slots and the motor window (US 7 to 9) is open item S26.","7. Body variants for sizes other than US 9: the values per size are the table of the last section (US 7 to 13) and the per-size files of design/mfg/parts/index.csv (items 96 to 98); the export is done. The sealant of the floor slots and the motor window (US 7 to 9) is 3M Scotch-Weld DP420 Black (item 45).",LD+"'items 96, 97, 98', 'item 45'"),
(F,"11. The 0.205 mm ring of metal between each microphone seat and hole is below the 0.30 mm floor rule: the body maker must accept it (17.24, open item S23).","11. The 0.205 mm ring of metal between each microphone seat and hole is below the 0.30 mm floor rule: the body maker must accept it (17.24, open item S23); it stays as a stated local exception, pass 0.17 to 0.23 mm at 4 points on the first body (item 77).",LD+"'item 77'"),
(F,"12. Sealing of the glass seat (seal SEAL1 in a seat lowered 0.05 mm), of the floor slots and of the joystick pocket (dam DAM1) is open item S26 (17.23); no rating can be claimed yet.","12. Sealing: the glass seat takes the seal SEAL1 (tesa 61305, 50 um, in a seat lowered 0.05 mm; item 110), the floor slots take 3M Scotch-Weld DP420 Black (item 45); the dam DAM1 of the joystick pocket is open item S26 (17.23). Version 1 claims no water or dust rating.",LD+"'item 110', 'item 45', 'item 101'"),
(F,"the adhesive of the two bond planes (X -8.60 and Y 2.05) and the seal of the two seams are not chosen; the body maker and the resin maker answer (architecture S24).","the adhesive of the two bond planes (X -8.60 and Y 2.05) and the seal of the two seams are not chosen; the body maker and the resin maker answer (architecture S24). The resin is Master Bond EP30Med, as the liner: RC1 is cast on its own and bonded to the body before the board goes in (assembly.md step 10).",LD+"'resin radio corner RC1, how it is made' 2026-11-13 04:28"),
(F,"cut away from the metal body on the planes X -8.60 and Y 2.05 and made as a bonded resin part in the body's colour,","cut away from the metal body on the planes X -8.60 and Y 2.05 and made as a bonded resin part (Master Bond EP30Med, cast on its own) in the body's colour,",LD+"'resin radio corner RC1, how it is made'"),
